<title>POLAND: BRE RAISES SHORT-TERM ZLOTY DEPOSIT RATES.</title>
<headline>BRE RAISES SHORT-TERM ZLOTY DEPOSIT RATES.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA (BRE) said in a Wednesday statement it had raised as of March 20 interest rates on one- two- and three-month zloty deposits and lowered interest on nine-month zloty deposits.</p>
<p>It said it had raised interest on one-month deposits by 0.3 point to 19.05 percent, on two-month deposits by 0.51 point to 19.26 percent and on three-month deposits by 0.76 point to 19.26 percent.</p>
<p>It lowered interest on nine-month deposits by 0.45 point to 18.8 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
